 "note": "The estates panel of 31 December 1415, read the day before this save: the crown holds about a quarter of the power of the state, the dhimmī 22%, the burghers 19%, the umarāʾ 18%, the ʿulamāʾ 10%, the commoners 2%, and the tribes, new with the Canaries, under 1%. Fourteen months after the Jamāʿa the umarāʾ are a quarter content and recovering, with Prince Yūsuf appeasing them in the dīwān. On 11 June 1415 the Ṭāʾifa of Shalamanka was taken into the crown after its ruler's death, and Maxorata in the Canaries was settled. The crown holds 184 towns and 2,445,000 people directly, with eight ṭāʾifas. Treasury 1,923, income 251 against 232; the realm's peace is still shaken.",
